<pdd-reason>Build Rust binaries outside the source tree using standard Ubuntu GTK development dependencies.</pdd-reason>
Implement build.sh with bash strict mode. Discover project root relative to the script, require pkg-config gtk+-3.0. If system metadata is missing, use the existing user-cache personal-files/gtk-dev/usr/lib/$(gcc -print-multiarch)/pkgconfig, or print the apt dependency instruction and fail. Respect existing PKG_CONFIG_PATH, XDG_CACHE_HOME and CARGO_TARGET_DIR. Default outputs to user cache personal-files/target, never create a repo target/ tree. Run cargo build --locked --release against this project's manifest. Print final binary path. No sudo or automatic system package installation.
